Battery menu: list a device's battery only once it is there.

The touchscreen (ELAN9008:00 04F3:4359) can take a pen, so it declares a pen battery, and the
kernel adds one for it whether or not a pen was ever used: "ELAN9008:00 04F3:4359 Stylus" at 0%,
not present. Neither the kernel nor UPower can hide it. So the battery list leaves out devices'
batteries (not the laptop's own) while they aren't present, and adds each as soon as it is: the
pen's once a pen reports its charge (kernel, hidinput_update_battery()).

To list them all again, set HideAbsentDeviceBatteries=false in the [Battery] group of
~/.config/danylo-tweaksrc (System Settings > Danylo's Linux Tweaks > Power & Battery), read when
Plasma starts.

Applied by scripts/patches/patch-library, see scripts/configure_hardware.

diff --git a/components/batterycontrol/batterycontrol.cpp b/components/batterycontrol/batterycontrol.cpp
